---
description: Require security and testing depth proportional to Capacitor and OTA release risk
alwaysApply: true
---

capacitor-security-and-testing:

- Never store credentials, auth tokens, or secrets in plain storage or logs.
- Enforce HTTPS-first networking and production-safe transport configuration.
- Disable WebView debugging and verbose native logs in release builds.
- Run security scanning for release candidates and block on high/critical findings.
- Match tests to risk: unit for logic, integration for bridge behavior, E2E for user flows.
- Validate rollback behavior on both iOS and Android before production promotion.
- Require at least one cold-start verification per platform after update publication.
- For auth/onboarding/payment updates, include explicit regression tests.
- Verify source maps and monitoring are wired before broad rollout.
